 Problem Statement
You need to design a Logger System that follows the Singleton Pattern to ensure there is only one instance of the logger throughout the application.

🛠 Requirements
The logger must only have one instance (no matter how many times it is accessed).

It should provide a method to log messages.

It should store logs in memory and allow retrieving all logs.

(Bonus) Add thread safety so multiple threads don’t create multiple instances.

(Bonus) Save logs to a file instead of just in memory.
